course: dictionary
lesson: 13574
title: Words that glow and burn
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in one go. Incandescent means giving out bright light because something is very hot. «The metal bar glowed incandescent in the furnace.» Picture a bar of metal so hot that it shines orange-white. That is what incandescent means.
explain: The word also has a second meaning in stories. «Dad was incandescent with rage when he saw the muddy footprints on the carpet.» Nobody is glowing here. Incandescent means extremely angry. The words «with rage» are a clue, because rage is a very strong kind of anger.
explain: Read the words around the word to check. In a science lesson, the sentence will be about heat, wires or light. In a story, the sentence will be about strong feelings. Then swap in your meaning: does «glowing with heat» or «furious» still make sense? If it does, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Incandescent means giving out bright light because it is very hot.
fact: In an incandescent light bulb, a thin wire gets very hot and glows.
fact: Incandescent bulbs waste much of their energy as heat, so many have been replaced by LED bulbs.
fact: «Incandescent with rage» means extremely angry, or furious.
fact: Lava and hot metal can be incandescent, and they can also be very bright and full of feeling in a story.
exercise: «The lava flowed down the mountain, glowing and incandescent.» What does incandescent mean here? | Cold and dark | Very quiet | *Glowing bright with heat | Slow and sticky
exercise: «Dad was incandescent when he saw the mud on the carpet.» What does incandescent mean? | Very tired and sleepy | *Extremely angry | Happy to see the mud | Calm and relaxed
exercise: «The old bulb glowed incandescent because the wire inside was hot.» Which word tells you why the bulb glows? | glowed | bulb | wire | *hot
test: «Mum was incandescent with rage.» What does this mean? | *Furious, full of anger | Half asleep | Happy and singing | Cold and wet
test: In a science lesson, why does an incandescent bulb waste energy? | It is too small to work properly | *Its hot wire gives off much energy as heat | It runs on water | It has been painted in bright colours
exam: Lara says, «The sunset was incandescent, red and gold across the sky.» What does incandescent mean here? | Wet and cold | Quiet and still | *Very bright and brilliant | Dark and cloudy
